index 081fa90..2305f41 100644
--- a/docs/proration.md
+++ b/docs/proration.md
@@ -13,8 +13,19 @@ from the morning of the change date, so that day counts as time left on the peri
 change on the first day of a period therefore credits the old price in full and charges
 the new price in full.
 
-The amount is `price * days left / days in period`, rounded to a whole minor unit in the
-default rounding mode. The credit and the charge are rounded separately.
+The charge is `price * days left / days in period`, rounded to a whole minor unit in the
+default rounding mode (half-even).
+
+The credit is the same share of what the customer actually paid for the old terms
+over that stretch, after any discount. Without a discount that is the same as
+`price * days left / days in period`. With a discount the customer gets back the
+discounted amount, never more than they paid, and never more than is left after any
+earlier credit on that charge. The new charge is discounted in the same way as any
+other charge in the period. If the old terms were themselves charged part-way through
+the period, the share is counted over the stretch that charge covered.
+
+The credit goes back at the tax rate it was charged at. Only the new charge uses the
+rate in force on the day of the change.
 
